            "and are not in this sample. includeTotals is assumed on, which is what the "
            "sample shows -- with it off the nine money/coverage fields are null by "
            "construction and this entry would flag, correctly.\n\n"
            "EXPECTED TO RE-FLAG ON A SCHEDULE, AND THAT IS THE POINT: the nine totals fields "
            "track an in-progress election period (candidate_election_year 2030, coverage "
            "2025-01-01 -> the last filed quarter), so the FEC moves them at every quarterly "
            "filing deadline. A buyer reads this block to decide whether to pay, so stale "
            "money columns are exactly the defect class cycle 1988 built this check for -- the "
            "remedy when it flags is to refresh the nine README values from live, NOT to "
            "loosen or drop this entry.\n\n"
            "**Found a real defect on first run (8th of 11 extensions to find one, same "
            "silent-value-drift class as 1991's wage-determination revisionNumber/dates):** "
            "all seven money fields plus coverageEndDate had gone stale since the row was "
            "captured -- receipts 4413931.4 -> 4965731.1, disbursements 4109645.05 -> "
            "5387108.74, cashOnHandEnd 3754333.02 -> 3028669.03 (down, not up: disbursements "
            "outran receipts this period, so a buyer eyeballing the old row would have read "
            "the trend backwards), individualContributions 4234605.7 -> 4770772.73, itemized "
            "1373252.85 -> 1679286.15, unitemized 2861352.85 -> 3091486.58, refunded 30368.08 "
            "-> 36068.43, coverageEndDate 2026-06-30 -> 2026-09-30. All twelve identity fields "
            "matched exactly, which is what localises the drift to the totals call. The same "
            "stale snapshot was also quoted in three places in the "
            "site/content/blog/fec-campaign-finance-json-api-demo-key.md post -- fixed there "
            "too in the same cycle (check-blog-claims does not read raw JSON snippets)."
        ),
    },
    {
        "slug": "eu-ted-tenders-scraper",
        "heading": "Sample row (real output, German construction-engineering notice)",
        "key_field": "publicationNumber",
        # Verified live cycle 2001 against the README's own sample (publication-number
        # 596425-2026). Keyless POST, endpoint proven live at cycle 2000. All 25 raw fields
        # dumped and hand-matched against main.js's normalize() before adding this entry.
        "fetch": fetch_ted_notice_row,
        "fields": {
