            # main.js firstValue(): array[0] ?? null, else the scalar itself.
            "buyerEmail": ted_first,
            "buyerPhone": ted_first,
            "buyerUrl": ted_first,
            # main.js: (typeof v === 'number' && v >= 0) ? v : null.
            "totalValue": lambda v: v if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool) and v >= 0 else None,
        },
        "skip_note": (
            "daysUntilDeadline MUST stay unchecked -- the README itself says it is computed "
            "at run time in Brussels local time and shrinks (or goes negative) every day, so "
            "it is unconditionally uncheckable against a fixed sample, not merely skipped for "
            "convenience.\n\n"
            "**Found a real defect on first run (9th of 12 extensions to find one, a NEW "
            "class -- the DATE is right but its own provenance LABEL is wrong):** "
            "deadlineType read 'tender' in the README but live is 'generic' -- "
            "deadline-receipt-tender-date-lot is null on this notice (confirmed live), so "
            "pickDeadline() falls through to deadline-date-lot, which is exactly the 'generic' "
            "leg, not 'tender'. deadlineDate itself ('2026-09-16') matches byte-for-byte "
            "either way, which rules out ordinary schedule drift (a drifted value would have "
            "moved the date, not just its label) and points to the label being typed wrong "
            "by hand when the sample was captured -- same hand-edit-not-drift conclusion as "
            "1992's clinicaltrials timeFrame, reached the same way (one field's value is "
            "self-consistent, a sibling field describing it is not). Fixed the README's "
            "deadlineType to 'generic'."
